// install_directory_owned_command (mode/owner/group/path -> rendered install text) is DELETED here:
// its one body was the exact composition shell_privileged_command_text_of_argv(coreutils_install_
// directory_owned_argv(...)) that gunbc.live_deploy.emit install_d_owned_for_user now spells
// directly against the argv authorities -- a second spelling of the same install words (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority). It had
// no production consumer (grep-verified). The live ACT on an owned-directory leaf goes through the
// ONE provider, gunbc.owned_directory owned_directory_ensure -- called for every ApplyLegEnsureDirectory
// by gunbc.host.host_effect_realize live_deploy_apply_ensure_directory_on_host and by
// gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dashboard_instance_apply. The roadmap node "Realize live_deploy's
// install-owned leaves as typed fs writes with an ownership effect" is REALIZED THERE at an
// ESTABLISHED RUNG (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder, review 90635): the acting route re-observes and re-decides at apply time
// and refuses a handover between the handover baseline and the act re-read
// (owned_directory_act_time_handover); today every caller passes no carried plan reading, so the
// window established by executed evidence is the decide-to-act window inside the provider call.
// The node stays OPEN with its next rung stated: thread the release_member_plan's own observation
// into owned_directory_ensure's plan_reading to cover the full plan-to-apply window. What remains in gunbc.live_deploy.emit is a DISPLAY surface --
// the same argv authority's words rendered as text (kept by the pinned witness, inert by admission,
// its refusal a false command) -- not an acting route.
